  "worked_solution": "To factor a sum of squares, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+25{n}^{2} & ={m}^{2}-(-25{n}^{2}) \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-(25{i}^{2}{n}^{2}) \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-(5in)^{2} \\\\  & =(m+5in)(m-5in)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
